Define "junk".

I consider Fire Brand, and Frost Brand to be junk,
except perhaps in exotic special circumstances,
because they're not weapons I would use.  I'd
choose any decent non-artifact weapon over them
in virtually any situation.

Demonbane, Vorpal Blade, and Sunsword are IMO
only a little better than a non-artifact longsword -- but
the longsword is one of the best non-artifact weapons
in the game; even a mundane one is better than a lot
of non-longsword artifact weapons, so it's perfectly
reasonable, if you happen to have one of these and
can reach at least skilled, and if you've no reason to
expect to get something better (e.g., you don't want
to wish for an artifact weapon or have a shortage of
wishes or have seen too many artifacts already to
bother trying), to go ahead and enchant it up to +7
and wield it for the rest of the game.  So I guess I
wouldn't classify them as junk.  But I also wouldn't
classify them as really *good* artifacts, because
some of the others are so much better.

Come to think of it, I guess that goes for Giantslayer
as well, if it comes to that.  I mean, sure, giants aren't
most of what threatens you (especially if titans don't
count), but it's still a longsword.  If "junk" means worse
than a non-artifact weapon, then I guess Giantslayer
doesn't really qualify.  It's not worse in any way I
can see, either.  (Its artifact properties sure aren't
very special, though.)

So I guess I'd divide artifact weapons into three
categories:

Junk:  not something I'd ever use, these are
actually worse than a good non-artifact weapon
(e.g., mundane longsword), either because they're
wimpy (e.g., Sting) or because they're more
trouble than they're worth (the most egregious
example being Stormbringer, but anything that
destroys useful stuff from monster inventory
belongs here too in my book).

Mediocre: at least as good as a good non-artifact
weapon, but not very much better, or only better
to any significant extent in narrow circumstances
(e.g., against specific classes of monsters).
Most of the artifact longswords are in this category.

Good: gets bonus damage and to-hit against
all or nearly all enemies (e.g., against all monsters
that aren't specifically foo resistant) and/or provides
significant useful properties when wielded (e.g., good
resistances you might not otherwise have), with no
really major downsides.  (Very minor downsides,
like Excalibur's, are acceptable, especially if
balanced by positive properties.)


